🧾 Problem Statement

You are given an integer array nums of size n.

You are allowed to choose at most one distinct value x from the array and remove all occurrences of x from nums.

After performing this operation (or choosing not to remove any element), your task is to find the maximum possible sum of a contiguous subarray from the resulting array.

Return the maximum subarray sum achievable.

⚠️ Important Notes
Removing a value x means all elements equal to x are deleted
The remaining elements retain their original order
The resulting subarray must still be contiguous in the modified array
You may also choose not to remove any element
📥 Input Format
First line: Integer n — size of the array
Second line: n space-separated integers representing nums
📤 Output Format
A single integer — the maximum subarray sum after applying the operation optimally
🧪 Example 1

Input

6
1 -2 3 4 -2 3

Output

11